ss\n\n**5. (MED) — Section 2 / Module 10 / Refrigerant Leak Detection**\nFinding: Propane sensor mounted at \"lowest point\" but R290 is lighter than air\nEvidence: \"mounted at the lowest point of the compressor compartment where propane accumulates\"\nRoot cause: refrigerant_properties.json has wrong density_vs_air for R290\nFix: Correct R290 density to 0.51 (lighter than air), update mounting guidance\n\n**6. (MED) — Section 1 / Brief & Requirements**\nFinding: BS EN 378-1 listed twice in compliance table with different descriptions\nEvidence: \"BS EN 378\" and \"BS EN 378-1\" both appear as separate entries\nRoot cause: standards_registry.yaml has duplicate entries with different keys\nFix: Consolidate to single \"BS EN 378\" entry covering all parts\n\n**7. (MED) — Section 2 / Module 3 / Expansion Vessel Assembly**\nFinding: 8L expansion vessel undersized for 200L cylinder + radiator circuit\nEvidence: \"Zilmet expansion vessel tank... 8 L volume\"\nRoot cause: hydronic_sizing() only calculating for cylinder volume, not total system\nFix: Update to include estimated radiator circuit volume (typically 50-100L additional)\n\n**8. (LOW) — Section 2 / Module 8 / Temperature Probes**\nFinding: NTC thermistors attributed to wrong manufacturer\nEvidence: \"TE Connectivity ntc thermistor probe (part NTCLE100E3103JB0)\"\nRoot cause: parts_lookup() matching on partial SKU without verifying manufacturer\nFix: Add manufacturer validation to parts_lookup() before assigning\n\n**9. (LOW) — Section 2 / Module 11 / Indoor Thermostat**\nFinding: Modbus baud rate 9600 too slow for 5-second polling with 144 parameters\nEvidence: \"2-wire RS485 Modbus RTU link at 9600 baud, with automatic polling every 5 seconds\"\nRoot cause: comms_sizing() using outdated baud rate defaults\nFix: Update default Modbus baud to 19200 or 38400 for modern systems\n\n**10. (MED) — Section 2 / Module 2 / Defrost System**\nFinding: 150W basepan heater insufficient for -25°C operation on 8kW unit\nEvidence: \"150 W silicone-sheathed basepan heater cable rated for -25°C\"\nRoot cause: defrost_sizing() using fixed wattage instead of scaling with capacity\nFix: Scale basepan heater to 25W/kW thermal (200W for 8kW unit)\n\n**11. (HIGH) — Appendix A / Parts Pending Verification**\nFinding: 60 unverified parts including critical safety components\nEvidence: \"60 part numbers could not be verified... Stripped (fakes): 60\"\nRoot cause: parts_generator() creating fabricated SKUs instead of querying real catalogs\nFix: Implement mandatory catalog API lookup before SKU generation\n\n**12. (MED) — Section 2 / Module 5 / Heat Exchangers**\nFinding: Evaporator and condenser both sized at generic \"8 kW\" without conditions\nEvidence: \"SWEP (Dover) brazed plate condenser... 8 kW thermal\"\nRoot cause: heat_exchanger_sizing() not specifying temperature conditions\nFix: Add explicit conditions (A7/W35 for heating, A35/W7 for cooling)\n\n**13. (LOW) — Section 2 / Module 7 / Fluid Kinematics**\nFinding: 500mm fan diameter excessive for 8kW domestic unit\nEvidence: \"500 mm composite axial fan blade\"\nRoot cause: fan_sizing() using commercial/industrial correlations\nFix: Add residential size limits (typically 350-450mm max for 8kW)\n\n**14. (MED) — Section 2 / Module 9 / Main Controller**\nFinding: STM32F407 overkill for heat pump control (168 MHz Cortex-M4)\nEvidence: \"STM32F407VGT6 ARM Cortex-M4 microprocessor operating at 168 MHz\"\nRoot cause: mcu_selection() defaulting to high-end without considering application\nFix: Add application-specific MCU selection (STM32F0/L0 adequate for HVAC)\n\n**15. (HIGH) — Section 2 / Module 3 / Hydronic Loop**\nFinding: No isolation valves specified for service/maintenance\nEvidence: Module 3 lists manifold and pump but no shut-off valves\nRoot cause: hydronic_components() missing mandatory service valves\nFix: Add ball valves to component list for flow/return isolation","refusal":null,"reasoning":null}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":40977,"compl